														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1581837">
									

<p>I liked the idea of metamorphosis in a group of organisms that generally don't undergo metamorphosis. I liked the visceral and somewhat gory cycle, especially the cannabalistic touch.</p>
<p>But it was the interview that sealed the deal. I don't think it needs any clarification at all; the sweet horror at realizing what &quot;we all knew it could happen, eventually&quot; means was excellent. And that she remembers? And that it's a pronghorn now so that means the Foundation probably did nothing to help her when she was literally being torn apart from the inside? Just the right amount of detail there and each bit keeps adding.</p>
<p>Overall it is a tad long. I liked the bit about moving to an oceanic facility, but some of the other containment details could be omitted or condensed - the observation walkway and some of the detail about the vets, for example.</p>

